true.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Asset | `campaign-archive-v1.tar.gz`, 62,575,902 bytes |\n| Asset SHA-256 | `62f1ef1875eaf54100c78fe26164b31d62b5efecfb4740e22a4e2a3c313bf918` |\n| Extracts to | 67 files, 277,466,583 bytes |\n| Tree fingerprint | `c3b79a0766c1d48117995826a2ee48a1f0b2a1955931f314a9d298dbc9611821` |\n\nContents: the campaign report, tables, audit and frozen manifest; per-setting\nrosters carrying every rostered method's untouched-test predictions, per-cell\nerror metrics and circuit-evaluation ledger; per-setting records carrying role\nassignments, counts, selected configurations and predictions; the fit bindings;\nand each setting's dataset manifest. Twelve settings: two regimes by three seeds\nby two training sizes.\n\nThe generated item streams and sidecars are excluded at 771 MB. The deterministic\ngenerators in this repository reproduce them from the recorded seed and\ndependency lock, and `report.json` carries the twelve dataset hashes a\nregeneration must match.\n\nTo verify:\n\n```\nsha256sum campaign-archive-v1.tar.gz\ntar -xzf campaign-archive-v1.tar.gz\ncd campaign-archive-v1 && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt\n```\n\nAll 67 lines report `OK`. `campaign-archive/` in the repository carries the same\nmanifest and checksum list, so the archive can be checked against a copy that\ntravels in git rather than one that travels beside the download.\n\nThe circuit-evaluation ledger counts in each roster entry are each method's own\ndeclaration and are audited nowhere; read them as declared cost rather than\nmeasured cost. `MANIFEST.md` states the archive's limits in full.\n"}]